{
	"Name": "Okta - Admin & Configuration Changes - Okta Admin Role Granted to a New User",
	"Description": "Alert: Okta\nGroup: Admin & Configuration Changes\nMITRE ATT&CK: Persistence / T1098.003\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta Admin Role Granted to a New User\" or \"<ip>|Okta Admin Role Granted to a New User\"\n\nAn administrator role granted (user.account.privilege.grant) to a user account created in the 24 hours before the search window (user.lifecycle.create). Creating an account and immediately making it an admin is a classic persistence step after an admin compromise.",
